--help prints the flags and exits with 0.
-- args --
plan --help
-- in/libc/BUILD.bazel --
-- stderr --
Usage of bazel-move-targets plan:
  -alias_for_rule_kind value
    	rule kind that leaves an alias() behind
  -alias_targets value
    	rule or extra names that leave an alias() behind
  -dst_package string
    	subpackage to move rules into, e.g. //foo/bar (required)
  -exclude value
    	rule names to remove from the directory selection
  -extra_names value
    	OLD or OLD=NEW: names with no literal rule (made by macros or comprehensions) that move too
  -file_attrs value
    	attributes whose bare strings are files, in addition to the defaults
  -include value
    	rule names to add to the directory selection
  -include_name_prefix value
    	also select rules without files whose names start with this prefix
  -label_attrs value
    	attributes whose bare strings are labels, in addition to the defaults
  -local_repo_names value
    	repository names that refer to this workspace: foo for @foo//...
  -move_statements value
    	FIRST-LAST: line range of top-level statements to move verbatim
  -out string
    	config file to write (default: stdout)
  -output_attrs value
    	attributes that name the files a rule generates, in addition to the defaults
  -package_comment string
    	comment line for a new destination BUILD file
  -package_relative_attrs value
    	attributes that are relative to the package directory and are reported when moved, in addition to the defaults
  -refuse_rule_kind value
    	rule kind never to move, in addition to the defaults
  -rename_strip_package_prefix value
    	prefix to strip from moved rule names; the longest match wins; "auto" derives prefixes from the destination directory (without a leading src/, as LLVM-libc names it)
  -src_package string
    	package to move rules out of, e.g. //foo (required)
  -strict_source_directories
    	require files to be directly in the destination directory
  -targets value
    	explicit rule names (disables directory selection); @FILE reads whitespace-separated names from FILE
  -verbose
    	also print informational items
  -workspace_root string
    	workspace directory (required)
